Day 36: The God Who Remembers You | Wednesday of the Fifth Week of Lent (Lent Devotional)

📌 YouTube Description
“I have engraved you on the palms of My hands.”
Not written lightly.
Not sketched in pencil.
Engraved — held permanently, intimately, unforgettably.

Welcome to Day 36 of our Lent journey.
Today’s reflection draws you into the tender, faithful heart of God — a God who never overlooks you, never forgets you, never loses track of your heart. Even when you feel unseen or unnoticed, you are held in His hands and carried in His love.

This spoken‑word devotional reminds you that God’s faithfulness is not fragile. It does not fade with time or weaken with distance. You are remembered because you belong to Him — always, fully, completely.

In today’s reflection, you’ll hear:

Why God’s remembrance is personal, intimate, and unwavering

How He sees you even when the world moves too quickly

Why Lent brings you back to the truth that you are held and known

A prayer to trust God’s steady faithfulness

A simple daily activity: whispering, “Lord, thank You for remembering me.”

